      "content": "that makes sense. but i'm worried about the \"unlikely to have occurred by chance alone\" part. how do statisticians actually account for the \"chance\" or the \"noise\" in the data that might mess with the results? like, what exactly is the underlying mechanism that makes a result significant or not? i want to be able to explain why the noise doesn't just invalidate the whole thing.",
